eight=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Smartphone revolt </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/0sN1fy6NrKG_EM6n_1CnVkqnWIo=/1920x1080/smart/2023/05/08/213928-1683581968420.gif\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of a manicured hand holding a phone with a spinning black and white vortex on the screen\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>Roughly half of American adults </strong>say they spend too much time on their phones — and more than half of younger adults are trying to kick the habit, <em>according to Pew Research Center <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.\" target=\"_blank\">data</a> out this week.</em></p><ul><li><strong>Why it matters: </strong>Over the past two decades, smartphones have come to dominate daily life. Now Americans — especially younger adults — are pushing back against how much of their time and attention they command.</li></ul><p><strong>🧠 The big picture: </strong>Excessive smartphone use among kids and adults has come under growing scrutiny, with studies linking it to problems ranging from \"<a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly9wbWMubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi9hcnRpY2xlcy9QTUM5OTgyODUwLz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB5f9d0e51\" target=\"_blank\">text neck</a>\" to <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmF0dXJlLmNvbS9hcnRpY2xlcy9zNDE1OTgtMDIzLTM2MjU2LTQ_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBd0e1f470\" target=\"_blank\">reduced cognitive performance</a> to <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly9wbWMubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi9hcnRpY2xlcy9QTUMxMjY3NDY3NC8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB30fd826c\" target=\"_blank\">relationship trouble</a>.</p><ul><li><strong>For kids, </strong>the concerns have led schools to <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjUvMDYvMDYvc2Nob29sLXBob25lLWJhbnMtZGMtbWFwLWJpcGFydGlzYW4_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB139a6bec\" target=\"_blank\">ban phones</a> and governments to <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMDYvMTUvdWstbWlub3JzLXNvY2lhbC1tZWRpYS1iYW5zP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB6bdc1e54\" target=\"_blank\">restrict social media</a>.</li><li><strong>For adults, </strong>there's a growing market of products, apps and <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMDQvMDUvcGhvbmUtZnJlZS1yZXN0YXVyYW50cy1iYXJzLWJhbnMtcmVzdHJpY3Rpb25zLW9mZmxpbmU_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBd25f5cdc\" target=\"_blank\">physical spaces</a> designed to keep us off our devices.</li></ul><p><strong>By the numbers: </strong>53% of U.S. adults say they're on their phones too much. That share jumps to 70% when looking just at 18- to 29-year-olds.</p><ul><li><strong>45% of all adults </strong>say they've tried to cut back on phone time in the last year. When considering just those under 50, the share is 58%.</li></ul><p><strong>📰 The other side: </strong>People want time back from their phones, but they do acknowledge some perks of the devices, Pew found.</p><ul><li><strong>73% say smartphones</strong> help keep them informed, and 51% say they help them stay connected to others.</li></ul><p><em>Go deeper: <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjIvMDYvMDgvZGlnaXRhbC1kZXRveC1kaW5pbmctaXBob25lLWxvY2stYm94LXNjcmVlbi10aW1lP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB44b38d4f\" target=\"_blank\">Our tips for digital detox</a>.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtOGRmNmE3OWQtMDk0MC00YTJkLTgxZjgtNDMzNmE4NGE3MGIzLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB3d3b78ad\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 1 big thing: Smartphone revolt&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A1 big thing: Smartphone revolt%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-finish-line-8df6a79d-0940-4a2d-81f8-4336a84a70b3.html%3Fchunk%3D1%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story1\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      \r\n<tr><td height=\"20\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=\"ol-adpad\" style=\"padding: 20px 3.5% 0 3.5%;\"><p class=\"b\"\r\nstyle=\"-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100% !important; margin-bottom: 0 !important; font-size: 11px !important; letter-spacing: 1.4px; color: #008dc8; font-weight:700;\"\r\n>\r\nA MESSAGE FROM PEPSICO\r\n</p></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 20px 3.5%; line-height: 1.5;\"><span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size: 26px; color: #222222;  font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;  letter-spacing: -0.1px; line-height: 1.5;\">AI can create farm resiliency</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td>\r\n<a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL3Nwb25zb3JlZC9wdXR0aW5nLWZhcm1lcnMtZmlyc3Qtd2l0aC1haT9heGlvc19hZGxpbms9MSZ1dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBaa457124\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://tpc.googlesyndication.com/pageadimg/imgad?id=CICAgJCVuLfC5gEQARgBKAEyCJwAKeWwJCTE\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" /></a>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"15\" style=\"height: 15px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"v\" style=\"padding: 0 3.5%; line-height: 1.75;  font-size: 17px; font-family: Georgia, serif; line-height: 1.75; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px;\">\r\n<p>As farmers face more extreme weather, water stress and input cost uncertainty, PepsiCo sees AI as a tool for resilience.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Looking ahead:</strong> When AI can identify smarter data, climate risk becomes more visible and efficiency more actionable for farmers.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL3Nwb25zb3JlZC9wdXR0aW5nLWZhcm1lcnMtZmlyc3Qtd2l0aC1haT9heGlvc19hZGxpbms9MSZ1dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCaa457124\" target=\"_blank\">Read the Q&amp;A.</a></p>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0; border-bottom: 10px solid #f5f5f5;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  2. 📸 Pic to go! </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/O28dwUOfQ3iEecf5Nub-L1SXMiA=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/09/03/1788465873186.jpeg' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/O28dwUOfQ3iEecf5Nub-L1SXMiA=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/09/03/1788465873186.jpeg\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">Photo: Bob Schumacher</div><p><strong>North America's highest peak</strong> — designated <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubnBzLmdvdi9kZW5hL2xlYXJuL2hpc3RvcnljdWx0dXJlL21vdW50YWluLW5hbWUuaHRtP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBc5778f19\" target=\"_blank\">Mount McKinley</a> by the U.S. government and <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47345372.348852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudXNncy5nb3YvbmV3cy9mZWF0dXJlZC1zdG9yeS9vbGQtbmFtZS1vZmZpY2lhbGx5LXJldHVybnMtbmF0aW9ucy1oaWdoZXN0LXBlYWs_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB2587b9fc\" target=\"_blank\">Denali</a> by the state of Alaska — was captured by reader Bob Schumacher of Wheaton, Ill., this week.</p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td